       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). Even 3,200 mg/day is usually limited to supervised inpatient use. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
